                                                "sense_id": "766b3a48-9532-3701-b4c0-7bbbe858a4e5",
                                                "text": "These [the eyes of the nautilus] are the simplest eyes of any large living animal -- lensless 'pinholes' that project a hazy and rather dim image onto its retinas."
